This product embeds service models from botocore, the low-level core of the
AWS SDK for Python (boto3).

    botocore
    Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/boto/botocore

The models are in internal/aws/generic/models. They are gzipped copies of each
service's service-2.json and paginators-1.json from the pinned botocore wheel
named in scripts/models.sh, with the documentation strings removed. The models in models/limits keep only the
input members that carry limits. You may obtain a copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 at
http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

This product embeds parts of the Google API discovery documents that ship in the
google.golang.org/api module (Go client libraries for Google APIs).

    google-api-go-client
    Copyright 2011 Google LLC
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/googleapis/google-api-go-client

The documents are in internal/gcp/generic/docs. They are gzipped copies of the discovery documents
that apis.txt lists, from the module version go.mod pins, with the descriptions removed
(internal/gcp/generic/gen.go). The module has no document for a few APIs. For those, internal/gcp/generic/extra
holds the discovery document fetched from the API's own host (https://<api>.googleapis.com/$discovery/rest), one
made by extra/proto2disco.go from the protobuf definitions of the cloud.google.com/go client,
or one written by hand from that client's REST paths and messages. Those client libraries are Copyright Google
LLC, Apache License, Version 2.0.

This product also embeds data from the Azure REST API specifications.

    azure-rest-api-specs
    Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
    Licensed under the MIT License
    https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs

internal/azure/generic/specs.json.gz keeps, for the resource types listed in internal/azure/generic/services.txt,
only what the Azure engine needs from the pinned commit named in scripts/azure-specs.sh: API versions, which
operations are long-running, read-only and required property names, and name rules. No descriptions or
schemas are copied.
